G|0|0|2|0|0|Parity 1>=1 (JFB capped to 1 excerpt vs skeptic-connective unit); both connectives accurate/on-tension; Luther's argument is real (he did charge James with "ascribing justification to works") but skeptic.work misattributes it to "Preface to the New Testament" — the exact quoted line "flatly against St. Paul...in ascribing justification to works" is from his separate 1522 "Preface to the Epistle of James" (confirmed via pristinegrace.org), not the general NT preface (LW 35:357-362, home of the "strawy epistle" line); fix work/attribution field to the James preface. Deeper-learning pd_work (Matthew Henry on Jas 2:14, names Rahab alongside Abraham per bibliaplus.org/blueletterbible) and gotquestions.org/life-Rahab.html link both verified real and on-topic.
